    "faq_detail_diy_e8F6wh": {
      "type": "faq-detail-diy",
      "blocks": {
        "item_qitPfM": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What is the Ulike Air 10?",
            "content": "<p>Ulike's Air 10 is our<strong> fastest, safest, and most advanced</strong> IPL hair removal device. It features <strong>Dual Lights</strong> and salon-inspired <strong>SHR Mode</strong>, delivering visible results in just 2 weeks. With a powerful 26-joule energy output, the Air 10 effectively removes even the most stubborn, coarse hair.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_xie6Uz": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Can Ulike IPL devices be used every day?",
            "content": "<p>For optimal results, we recommend using Ulike IPL devices <strong>every other day for the first 4 weeks</strong>, followed by <strong>maintenance sessions once or twice a month</strong>. Treating the same area every day offers no additional benefits. Instead, you can alternate between different body parts on different days.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_fpAXDA": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How long does Ulike Air 10 take to work?",
            "content": "<p>With its Dual Lights and SHR Mode, the Air 10 provides visible hair reduction in just <strong>2 weeks</strong>. Most users achieve their desired results by the end of the recommended 12-week treatment cycle, resulting in smooth, hair-free skin. Individual results may vary based on factors like ethnicity, skin tone, hair color, and treatment area.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_VbRpWX": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Can Ulike IPL devices be used on intimate areas?",
            "content": "<p>Ulike IPL devices are suitable for most body areas. However, sensitive regions like the bikini line may require gentler hair removal methods. To address this, Ulike devices feature various comfort modes, including a lower power setting for sensitive areas. Note that IPL devices should not be used directly on the genitals, testicles, anus, or nipples.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_Mb7kFt": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Do I need to shave before using Ulike Air 10?",
            "content": "<p>Yes, it's important to shave any hair longer than <strong>2 mm</strong> in the treatment area. This allows the IPL light to target the hair root directly, as well as makes sessions more comfortable. Not shaving may lead to a burning smell during treatment, as the IPL light burns surface hair instead of reaching the follicles. Use shaving alone for preparation; other hair removal methods may reduce treatment effectiveness.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_Q9tLEM": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Are Ulike IPL hair removal devices FDA-cleared?",
            "content": "<p>Yes, all Ulike IPL hair removal devices are FDA-cleared, medically tested, and compliant with international standards. Our comprehensive in-house development process includes rigorous testing by international governing bodies. Ulike devices have received a lot of global certifications, guaranteeing a reliable hair removal experience from start to finish.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_kQLG7z": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How often should I use Ulike Air 10?",
            "content": "<p>To effectively target hair follicles during their anagen (growth) phase, we recommend a 12-week cycle: start with 3 treatments per week for the first 4 weeks, then switch to maintenance sessions once or twice a month. Adjust your treatment frequency based on your hair growth patterns, especially for areas with thicker or more stubborn hair. Always monitor your skin's response and make adjustments as needed to prevent discomfort.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_zqdUzz": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What is the difference between Air 10 and Air 3?",
            "content": "<p>The Air 10 is our next-generation IPL hair removal device, featuring Dual Lights, a wider treatment window, and SHR Mode for faster treatments and quicker results. Its powerful 26J output makes it highly effective for removing resilient, coarse hair. It also includes SkinSensor technology, which adjusts power output based on your skin tone.</p><p>The Air 3 is our iconic IPL hair removal device. Its compact design makes it easy to store and maneuver. While it lacks some advanced features like Dual Lights, SHR Mode, and SkinSensor, the Air 3 remains an affordable and effective solution for IPL hair removal.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_RHGHRV": {
          "type": "item",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/FAQS_3c69a52b-52ec-4567-8ec7-ce4a277cd176.jpg",
            "image1": "shopify://shop_images/FAQs-mobile_44504b31-28af-429c-95b5-6b0c4e93ea10.jpg",
            "title": "Can everyone use IPL?",
            "content": "<p>IPL (Intense Pulsed Light) hair removal works by emitting intense light pulses that are absorbed by the pigment in the hair follicles. The absorbed light is then converted into heat, which targets the hair follicles and inhibits future hair growth.<br/><br/>It is important to note that IPL is most effective on individuals with lighter skin tones and darker hair colors. This is because the light energy is primarily absorbed by the melanin pigment in the hair. In individual's skin that's rich in melanin, the excess melanin can also absorb the light energy, leading to potential skin damage.<br/><br/>Similarly, IPL may not be as effective on individuals with light hair colors such as blonde, gray, or red. This is because these hair colors have less melanin content, making it challenging for the IPL device to target the hair follicles effectively.<br/><br/>To ensure the effectiveness and safety of IPL hair removal, we recommend users to refer to our skin tone chart before making a purchase.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_cFQC6i": {
          "type": "item",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "title": "Who should not use IPL?",
            "content": "<p>Ulike IPL hair removal devices are not recommended for<br/>individuals with any of the following conditions:<br/><br/>- A known skin disorder<br/><br/>- Skin diseases such as allergic dermatitis or eczema<br/><br/>- Photosensitive epilepsy or photosensitivity<br/><br/>- Menstruating, pregnant, or lactating individuals<br/><br/>- Dark black or sunburnt skin (please refer to the skin tone chart)<br/><br/>- Broken skin, scabs, healed wounds, cancer, or hemangiomas<br/><br/>- Any artificial aesthetic, prosthetic, or plastic surgery area<br/><br/>- Tattooed areas</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_BMPyxw": {
          "type": "item",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "title": "Why choose IPL technology for hair removal?",
            "content": "<p>IPL, or intense pulsed light, uses strong pulses of broad-spectrum light to target hair at the root. The light is absorbed by the melanin in the hair follicle, where it is then converted into heat, resulting in thinner regrowth and eventually stopping hair growth altogether. Ulike IPL devices are FDA cleared and offer a cost-effective, convenient solution compared to a clinic laser and traditional methods of hair removal.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_kzJTLk": {
          "type": "item",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "title": "I have PCOS. Is it suitable for me?",
            "content": "<p>Our Air 10 IPL hair removal device is designed to provide long-term hair reduction, even for those with persistent or abnormal hair growth. We recommend consulting with a healthcare professional for specific PCOS related questions before beginning IPL treatment.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_3NCWma": {
          "type": "item",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "title": "When Can I See the Effect, and is it Permanent?",
            "content": "<p>Most customers start to see evident hair reduction after 3-4 weeks. With 2-3 treatment per week, the effect becomes completely evident after 12 weeks. After each treatment, hair will grow much more sparsely and thinly. Eventually, hair reduction becomes permanent. To maintain the skin’s smoothness, you need to do 1 treatment every 2 to 3 months or as required. Both the outcome and frequency of treatment are different case by case.</p><p> According to FDA’s regulations, permanent hair removal means ‘continued and steady reduction of hair over a prolonged period’, which we provide, though some may interpret the term ‘permanent’ differently. Please know that even the photo-therapy used in clinics is not entirely permanent.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_9F9MiF": {
          "type": "item",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "title": "Does IPL treatment hurt?",
            "content": "<p>IPL hair removal is generally considered to be much less painful and nearly as effective as laser hair removal. Additionally, Ulike is the only company that features Sapphire Ice Cooling  technology to ensure nearly painless sessions.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_knHd3A": {
          "type": "item",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "title": "Which Areas of the Body Can I Use This On?",
            "content": "<p>You can use your handset on any part of your body, including your Brazilian (Bikini area) and face. But please do not use around the eyes (use only below cheekbones)</p><p>Our IPL is not suitable for the ‘inner parts of the bikini area. Therefore you should never use it on the labia minora, vagina, scrotum, or anus.</p><p>To prevent discomfort, we advise you to treat the bikini area, inner thighs, and buttocks from the lowest intensity level, as the skin in these areas can be more sensitive.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_d7CDfr": {
          "type": "item",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "title": "Does IPL treatment hurt?",
            "content": "<p>IPL hair removal is generally considered to be much less painful and nearly as effective as laser hair removal. Additionally, Ulike is the only company that employs Sapphire Ice-Cooling  technology to ensure completely Painless sessions.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
